# `logs/` excluded the DIRECTORY, and git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is
# excluded -- so no negation could ever reach the eval artifacts, and the mirror's copy of
# this file made `git add -A` refuse all 91 of them on publish. Exclude the CONTENTS instead,
# then re-admit the one subtree the WHITE_PAPER cites by path. 1.8 MB, scanned for
# credentials and personal paths. Run traces, cloak audits and everything else stay out.
logs/*
!logs/eval_results/
logs/eval_results/*
!logs/eval_results/*.json
# The PB lock board -- the override guard's only input. Without it that CI job
# dies before checking a single compile.sh.
!logs/programbench_lock_board.json
