# ── Training corpora (large files — store on HuggingFace, not git) ───────────
# DO NOT "fix" this by deleting the pattern. It is load-bearing:
# corpus/programbench/training_corpus/pb_verdict_corpus.jsonl is 9.06 GB (measured
# 2026-07-29). GitHub rejects any single file over 100 MB, so tracking it is not
# merely inadvisable, it is impossible.
#
# But a blanket extension ban is a blunt instrument, and it was also swallowing small
# authoritative files that are unrecoverable if lost — they are gitignored, so there is
# no copy in history to restore from. Those are un-ignored explicitly below rather than
# by weakening the default deny.
*.jsonl

# Small, authoritative, and irreplaceable. Each is well under GitHub's limit and each is
# named "active / needed" by
# corpus/programbench/training_corpus/OFFLOADED_TO_T.md — which is precisely the file
# that documents which corpora were deliberately moved to T: and which must stay here.
!corpus/programbench/training_corpus/pb_negative_signal.jsonl

# Guard against the accident this whole block exists to prevent: if a negated file ever
# grows past what git should carry, `scripts/dev/gitignore_audit.py` fails and says so.



